{"key":"enterprise/T1486","id":"T1486","name":"Data Encrypted for Impact","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["impact"],"platforms":["ESXi","IaaS","Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may encrypt data on target systems or on large numbers of systems in a network to interrupt availability to system and network resources. They can attempt to render stored data inaccessible by encrypting files or data on local and remote drives and withholding access to a decryption key. This may be done in order to extract monetary compensation from a victim in exchange for decryption or a decryption key (ransomware) or to render…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1486","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--b80d107d-fa0d-4b60-9684-b0433e8bdba0","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.709Z","source_object_version":"1.5","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0023","name":"Cloud Storage Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0023","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--45977f14-1bcc-4ec4-ac14-a30fd3a11f44","page":"telemetry/DC0023/"},{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0215","name":"Detection of Multi-Platform File Encryption for Impact","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0215","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--d080a1b1-5ad1-45a1-8f7b-b736986c20d9","relationship_id":"relationship--245046a7-adc8-4a5a-84b4-e0af6c3b8dc7"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0602","name":"Analytic 0602","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0215#AN0602","guidance":"High-frequency file write operations using uncommon extensions, followed by ransom note creation, registry tampering, or shadow copy deletion. Often uses CLI tools like vssadmin, wbadmin, cipher, or PowerShell.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0215"},{"id":"AN0603","name":"Analytic 0603","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0215#AN0603","guidance":"Encryption via custom or open-source tools (e.g., openssl, gpg, aescrypt) recursively targeting user or system directories. Also includes overwrite of existing data and ransom note drops.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0215"},{"id":"AN0604","name":"Analytic 0604","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0215#AN0604","guidance":"Userland or kernel-level ransomware encrypting user files (Documents, Desktop) using `srm`, `gpg`, or compiled payloads. Often correlated with ransom note creation in multiple directories.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0215"},{"id":"AN0605","name":"Analytic 0605","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0215#AN0605","guidance":"Ransomware encrypts .vmdk, .vmx, .log, or VM config files in VMFS datastores. May rename to .locked or delete/overwrite with encrypted versions. Often correlates with shell commands run through `dcui`, SSH, or vSphere.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0215"},{"id":"AN0606","name":"Analytic 0606","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0215#AN0606","guidance":"Encryption of cloud storage objects (e.g.,